IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-required-information.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries), the cross-heading
-- "Notification of information about secretaries" continued: ss 279J, 279K and 279L (lines 3671-3705 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1 of the part agent coa6: what "the required information" about a secretary is.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa6-private-and-public.l4. JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE the text's no in its own words
-- (a "means" definition, "is" followed by a list, an "other than" exclusion, a "where"); NOTHING "not covered" (a grant limited by
-- its own wording, a point the text hands to another section or to regulations). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- SEAMS (inputs, named for the section that answers; this module imports coa-core only):
--   s 1088  whether the registrar is required, by regulations under s 1088(1)(a) or (b), to refrain from making a former name
--           available for public inspection or from disclosing it (coa23);
--   s 1141  whether an address is a service address (coa25);
--   s 3(1) and s 1158  whether the body corporate is a limited company, and a UK-registered company (the keel).
--
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (machinery, inert reason 2): the Secretary of State's powers by regulations in ss 279J(5) and 279K(2), and the
-- "affirmative resolution procedure" of ss 279J(6) and 279K(3). Their effect, if exercised, would change the lists below.

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Notification of information about secretaries`

-- ---- s 279J: Required information about a secretary etc: individuals -------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) who is an
-- individual is— (a) name; (b) any relevant former names; (c) a service address ...". "is" followed by a list is read as closed.
-- src:3672 | (1) The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) who is an individual is—
-- src:3673 | (a) name;
-- src:3674 | (b) any relevant former names;
-- src:3675 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”).
@ref s 279J(1) The required information about an individual: the items (src:3672-3675)
DECLARE `s 279J(1) item of the required information about an individual` IS ONE OF
    `s 279J(1)(a) name`
    `s 279J(1)(b) any relevant former names`
    `s 279J(1)(c) a service address`
    `s 279J(1) any other item`

-- src:3672 | (1) The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) who is an individual is—
-- src:3673 | (a) name;
-- src:3674 | (b) any relevant former names;
-- src:3675 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”).
@ref s 279J(1) Required information about a secretary etc: individuals (src:3672-3675)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279J(1) item of the required information about an individual`)
`s 279J(1) the required information about a secretary or joint secretary who is an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST (LIST `s 279J(1)(a) name`, `s 279J(1)(b) any relevant former names`, `s 279J(1)(c) a service address`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is an individual" (a body corporate or firm is s 279K)

-- src:3672 | (1) The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) who is an individual is—
-- src:3673 | (a) name;
-- src:3674 | (b) any relevant former names;
-- src:3675 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”).
@ref s 279J(1) Required information about a secretary etc: individuals (is an item part of it) (src:3672-3675)
GIVEN item IS A `s 279J(1) item of the required information about an individual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279J(1) the item is part of the required information about an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 279J(1) any other item` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The required information about a secretary or joint secretary ... who is an individual is— (a) name; (b) any relevant former names; (c) a service address"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1)(c): "a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”)". Whether an address is a service address is
-- s 1141 (coa25), an input.
-- src:3675 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”).
@ref s 279J(1)(c) A service address, which may be stated as the registered office (src:3675)
GIVEN `the statement of the service address` IS A STRING
      `s 1141 the address is a service address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279J(1)(c) the statement given is an acceptable statement of the service address` MEANS
    IF `the statement of the service address` EQUALS "The company’s registered office"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1141 the address is a service address`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "(c) a service address" (s 1141 says the address is not a service address)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1141 does not say whether the address is a service address

-- (3): "“former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes; “name” means the individual's
-- forename and surname."
-- src:3682 | (3) In this section—
-- src:3683 | “former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes;
@ref s 279J(3) "former name" (src:3682-3683)
GIVEN `the name is a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279J(3) the name is a former name` MEANS
    IF `the name is a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes"

-- src:3682 | (3) In this section—
-- src:3684 | “name” means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 279J(3) "name" (src:3682-3684)
DECLARE `s 279J(3) name` HAS
    `s 279J(3) forename` IS A STRING
    `s 279J(3) surname` IS A STRING

-- src:3682 | (3) In this section—
-- src:3684 | “name” means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 279J(3) "name" (the individual's name) (src:3682-3684)
GIVEN forename IS A STRING
      surname IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 279J(3) name`
`s 279J(3) the individual's name` MEANS `s 279J(3) name` OF forename, surname

-- (2): "In subsection (1)(b) “relevant former name” means any former name other than (a) in the case of a peer, or an individual
-- normally known by a British title, the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the
-- title, or (b) in the case of any person (i) a former name which was changed or disused before the person attained the age of 16
-- years, (ii) ... changed or disused for 20 years or more, or (iii) ... which the registrar is required to refrain from making
-- available for public inspection or from disclosing (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)."
-- "Before the person attained the age of 16" is read as strictly before the 16th birthday; "for 20 years or more" as the 20th
-- anniversary of the change or any day after it (forks F-16 and F-20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3676 | (2) In subsection (1)(b) “relevant former name” means any former name other than—
-- src:3677 | (a) in the case of a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title, the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title, or
-- src:3678 | (b) in the case of any person—
-- src:3679 | (i) a former name which was changed or disused before the person attained the age of 16 years,
-- src:3680 | (ii) a former name which has been changed or disused for 20 years or more, or
-- src:3681 | (iii) a former name which the registrar is required to refrain from making available for public inspection or from disclosing (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b).
@ref s 279J(2) "relevant former name" (src:3676-3681)
GIVEN `the name is a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a peer or is normally known by a British title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of birth of the individual` IS A DATE
      `the day the name was changed or disused` IS A DATE
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
      `s 1088 the registrar is required to refrain from making the former name available for public inspection or from disclosing it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279J(2) the former name is a relevant former name` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 279J(3) the name is a former name` `the name is a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant former name” means any former name" (and “former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes)
    ELSE IF `the individual is a peer or is normally known by a British title` AND `the name is the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than (a) in the case of a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title, the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title"
         ELSE IF `the day the name was changed or disused` LESS THAN `add years` `the date of birth of the individual` 16
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than ... (b) in the case of any person (i) a former name which was changed or disused before the person attained the age of 16 years"
              ELSE IF `add years` `the day the name was changed or disused` 20 AT MOST `the day of the question`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than ... (ii) a former name which has been changed or disused for 20 years or more"
                   ELSE CONSIDER `s 1088 the registrar is required to refrain from making the former name available for public inspection or from disclosing it`
                        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than ... (iii) a former name which the registrar is required to refrain from making available for public inspection or from disclosing (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)"
                        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1088 does not say whether the registrar is required to refrain

-- (4): a peer or an individual usually known by a title may give the title instead of the forename and surname. A grant ("may be
-- satisfied"): outside it the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:3685 | (4) Where a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, any requirement of this Act to provide the individual’s name because it forms part of the required information may be satisfied by providing that title instead of the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 279J(4) A title instead of the forename and surname (src:3685)
GIVEN `the individual is a peer or is usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title is provided instead of the individual's forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279J(4) the requirement to provide the name is satisfied by providing the title` MEANS
    IF `the individual is a peer or is usually known by a title` AND `the title is provided instead of the individual's forename and surname`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a secretary or joint secretary ... is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, any requirement ... to provide the individual’s name ... may be satisfied by providing that title instead of the individual’s forename and surname"

-- ---- s 279K: Required information about a secretary etc: corporate secretaries and firms -----------------------------------

-- (1): for "a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed": (a) corporate or firm name;
-- (b) principal office; (c) a service address; (d) "in the case of a limited company that is a UK-registered company, the registered
-- number"; (e) "in any other case, particulars of (i) the legal form ... and the law by which it is governed, and (ii) if
-- applicable, the register in which it is entered ... and its registration number in that register".
-- src:3691 | (1) The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, is—
-- src:3692 | (a) corporate or firm name;
-- src:3693 | (b) principal office;
-- src:3694 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”);
-- src:3695 | (d) in the case of a limited company that is a UK-registered company, the registered number;
-- src:3696 | (e) in any other case, particulars of—
-- src:3697 | (i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed, and
-- src:3698 | (ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register.
@ref s 279K(1) The required information about a body corporate or firm: the items (src:3691-3698)
DECLARE `s 279K(1) item of the required information about a body corporate or firm` IS ONE OF
    `s 279K(1)(a) corporate or firm name`
    `s 279K(1)(b) principal office`
    `s 279K(1)(c) a service address`
    `s 279K(1)(d) the registered number`
    `s 279K(1)(e)(i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed`
    `s 279K(1)(e)(ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`

-- src:3691 | (1) The required information about a secretary or joint secretary (or proposed secretary or joint secretary) that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, is—
-- src:3692 | (a) corporate or firm name;
-- src:3693 | (b) principal office;
-- src:3694 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”);
-- src:3695 | (d) in the case of a limited company that is a UK-registered company, the registered number;
-- src:3696 | (e) in any other case, particulars of—
-- src:3697 | (i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed, and
-- src:3698 | (ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register.
@ref s 279K(1) Required information about a secretary etc: corporate secretaries and firms (src:3691-3698)
GIVEN `the secretary is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3(1) the body is a limited company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the body is a UK-registered company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body or firm is entered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279K(1) item of the required information about a body corporate or firm`)
`s 279K(1) the required information about a secretary or joint secretary that is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the secretary is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed" (an individual is s 279J; a firm that is not a legal person is s 279L)
    ELSE IF (`s 3(1) the body is a limited company` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 1158 the body is a UK-registered company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST (LIST `s 279K(1)(a) corporate or firm name`, `s 279K(1)(b) principal office`, `s 279K(1)(c) a service address`, `s 279K(1)(d) the registered number`)
         ELSE IF (`s 3(1) the body is a limited company` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`s 1158 the body is a UK-registered company` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              THEN IF `the body or firm is entered in a register`
                   THEN JUST (LIST `s 279K(1)(a) corporate or firm name`, `s 279K(1)(b) principal office`, `s 279K(1)(c) a service address`, `s 279K(1)(e)(i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed`, `s 279K(1)(e)(ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`)
                   ELSE JUST (LIST `s 279K(1)(a) corporate or firm name`, `s 279K(1)(b) principal office`, `s 279K(1)(c) a service address`, `s 279K(1)(e)(i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed`)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 3(1) or s 1158 does not say whether the body is a limited company that is a UK-registered company, so (d) or (e) cannot be chosen

-- src:3694 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”);
@ref s 279K(1)(c) A service address, which may be stated as the registered office (src:3694)
GIVEN `the statement of the service address` IS A STRING
      `s 1141 the address is a service address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279K(1)(c) the statement given is an acceptable statement of the service address` MEANS
    `s 279J(1)(c) the statement given is an acceptable statement of the service address` `the statement of the service address` `s 1141 the address is a service address`

-- ---- s 279L: Firms all of whose partners are joint secretaries -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "This section applies where (a) all the members in a firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of a company,
-- and (b) the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed." The text's own "where": outside it, JUST FALSE.
-- src:3702 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:3703 | (a) all the members in a firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of a company, and
-- src:3704 | (b) the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed.
@ref s 279L(1) Firms all of whose partners are joint secretaries: when the section applies (src:3702-3704)
GIVEN `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279L(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of the company` AND `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where (a) all the members in a firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of a company, and (b) the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed"

-- (2): "Any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the required information about the members as joint secretaries ... may
-- instead be satisfied by providing the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been
-- appointed as secretary." A grant: outside its conditions the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:3702 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:3703 | (a) all the members in a firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of a company, and
-- src:3704 | (b) the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed.
-- src:3705 | (2) Any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the required information about the members as joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) may instead be satisfied by providing the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary.
@ref s 279L(2) The requirement may instead be satisfied by the firm's information (src:3702-3705)
GIVEN `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information provided is the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279L(2) the requirement is satisfied by providing the firm's information instead` MEANS
    IF       (`s 279L(1) this section applies` `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of the company` `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND `the information provided is the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may instead be satisfied by providing the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary"

-- What that information is: s 279K(1) for a firm treated as a legal person. A firm that is not a legal person is not a company, so
-- (d) "a limited company that is a UK-registered company" cannot apply and (e) "in any other case" does.
-- src:3705 | (2) Any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the required information about the members as joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) may instead be satisfied by providing the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary.
@ref s 279L(2) The information that would be required if the firm were a legal person (src:3705)
GIVEN `the firm is entered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279K(1) item of the required information about a body corporate or firm`)
`s 279L(2) the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and had been appointed as secretary` MEANS
    `s 279K(1) the required information about a secretary or joint secretary that is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `the firm is entered in a register`
